  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: around Sizzano AE 1999 (2002) no. 777a on p. 242 includes an inscribed cippus that served as a boundary marker of the Pagus Agaminus. The inscribed cippus was founded immured in a local parish church. Based on orthography, the stone dates to the late first or early second century.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
